#
# Debian control template for aphrody.
# The release pipeline (CI) substitutes __VERSION__ before calling `dpkg-deb`
# or passing --deb-version to `cargo deb`.
#
# Architecture note:
#   - Multi-arch package: amd64 (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu) + arm64
#     (aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu). The Debian convention is to declare both
#     architectures space-separated; cargo-deb / dpkg-deb emit one .deb per
#     target invocation:
#       cargo deb --target x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu   -> aphrody_1.0.0~canary_amd64.deb
#       cargo deb --target aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu  -> aphrody_1.0.0~canary_arm64.deb
#     The release pipeline runs both, then uploads both .deb assets to the
#     GitHub release.
#
# Depends note:
#   - libssl3 is provided by OpenSSL 3.x on Ubuntu 22.04+ / Debian 12+.
#     Ubuntu 26.04 ships OpenSSL 3.x as the default; no extra PPA needed.
#   - If a fully-static musl binary is produced (target x86_64-unknown-linux-musl
#     + CARGO_DEB_VARIANT=musl), libssl3 is NOT required; produce a separate
#     aphrody-musl package with Depends: libc6 only (musl is statically linked
#     into the binary itself via `features = ["vendored"]` on the openssl crate).

Package: aphrody
Version: 1.0.0~canary
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Maintainer: aphrody-code <noreply@aphrody-code.dev>
Description: Cross-platform Rust CLI (Linux / Windows / macOS / WebAssembly).
 Hermetic Google-grade supply chain.
 .
 aphrody is the primary entry point for the aphrody platform: forensics,
 A2A agent orchestration, MCP tool server, and monorepo mapper (mrx).
 Built with Rust nightly, Edition 2024. Verified with cargo-deny + cargo-vet.
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.38), libssl3 (>= 3.0)
Homepage: https://github.com/aphrody-code/aphrody
